  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our Plant-Based Living Series is a free ten-week email program full of simplified takeaways and actionable tips on healthy eating in the new year. Whether you’re new to a whole food, plant-based lifestyle or would benefit from reminders on some of the key aspects of healthy evidence-based nutrition, this series is for you. Each week, you will receive an email on topics like: dining by traffic light, nutritional considerations and concerns, disease prevention, and even a brand-new menu planning tool</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/plantbased-living-series/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sign up here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and share this new free resource with friends and family who are exploring plant-based eating in 2022.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Give the Gift of a Special Message</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71905 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/MG-Valentine-Flat-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/MG-Valentine-Flat-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/MG-Valentine-Flat-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/MG-Valentine-Flat-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/MG-Valentine-Flat-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/MG-Valentine-Flat-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/MG-Valentine-Flat-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/MG-Valentine-Flat.png 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>For Valentine’s Day, I’m recording personal video messages again! The first 50 people who donate $200 or more </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.app.neoncrm.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=67&amp;&amp;test=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">using this form</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> will be able to send in a personalized script that I’ll record for you or your loved one.  UPDATE: Thank you to everyone who donated; this opportunity is now closed for the year. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Key Takeaways: Microbiome</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/microbiome/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71829\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Microbiome.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Microbiome.png 800w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Microbiome-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Microbiome-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Microbiome-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Microbiome-540x540.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Day in and day out, trillions of good bacteria work in our gut, metabolizing, detoxifying, and activating important nutrients in our food. How do we keep these gut bugs happy so they help keep us healthy? Check out the videos on the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/microbiome/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">microbiome topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span></p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4><b>Recipe: Southwest Quinoa Stew</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/southwest-quinoa-stew/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71835 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/southwest-quinoa-stew-4-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/southwest-quinoa-stew-4-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/southwest-quinoa-stew-4-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/southwest-quinoa-stew-4-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/southwest-quinoa-stew-4-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/southwest-quinoa-stew-4-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/southwest-quinoa-stew-4-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/southwest-quinoa-stew-4-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>One way to support your microbiome is with the quinoa, beans, and sweet potatoes in this Southwest Quinoa Stew. Get the free recipe </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/southwest-quinoa-stew/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and watch a video of how it’s made on our </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CThkkRPgAiS/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instagram</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>2021 in Review</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/t5bdhwxtbbp26hjeje8n8utmfd7w744l\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71821\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/2021-YIR.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/2021-YIR.png 800w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/2021-YIR-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/2021-YIR-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/2021-YIR-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/2021-YIR-540x540.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Thank you for all of your support in 2021. To see what we accomplished last year, check out our 2021 Year in Review report. Highlights include launching our new outreach program that provided 5,000 free copies of our </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/healthkit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evidence-Based Eating Guide</span></i></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to health professionals, expanding our team, hitting more than 30 million video views, and reaching a million hard copies sold of </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Die</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Download the full report</span> <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/t5bdhwxtbbp26hjeje8n8utmfd7w744l\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4><b>Volunteer Spotlight: Cass Warbeck</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71837\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Warbeck-1024x1331.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"260\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Warbeck-1024x1331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Warbeck-960x1248.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Warbeck-768x998.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Warbeck-720x936.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Warbeck-540x702.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/Warbeck.png 1060w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>“I’ve been a proud volunteer at NutritionFacts for many years now! I started on the article retrieval team and now respond to comments on the Facebook page and help out with video review. I find it rewarding to contribute to an organization that highlights and shares such important nutrition research. This information should be accessible to all, and I believe that one day whole food, plant-based nutrition will be a fundamental component of standard healthcare. By volunteering, I know that I’m helping manifest that change. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I adore grapes and matcha! But one of my favourite recipes is a morning BROL bowl, based on Dr. Greger’s recipe, which has replaced standard oatmeal. I heat a cup of </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/basic-brol-barley-rye-oats-and-lentils/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">BROL</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> with soy milk and then spice it with cinnamon, cardamom, and cloves, and then add ground flaxseed, walnuts, amla powder, and blueberries. Top it with some hemp hearts, and you’ll be fueled for hours!”</span></p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-60211 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></h4>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/plant-based-eating-score-put-to-the-test/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70110\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-4-Plant-Based-Eating-Score-Put-to-the-Test-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Fresh plant based diet ingredients on light countertop\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-4-Plant-Based-Eating-Score-Put-to-the-Test-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-4-Plant-Based-Eating-Score-Put-to-the-Test-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-4-Plant-Based-Eating-Score-Put-to-the-Test-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-4-Plant-Based-Eating-Score-Put-to-the-Test-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-4-Plant-Based-Eating-Score-Put-to-the-Test-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-4-Plant-Based-Eating-Score-Put-to-the-Test-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-4-Plant-Based-Eating-Score-Put-to-the-Test-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-4-Plant-Based-Eating-Score-Put-to-the-Test.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/plant-based-eating-score-put-to-the-test/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Plant-Based Eating Score Put to the Test</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How can you get a perfect diet score?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-heal-a-leaky-gut-with-diet/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70128\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"High fiber super foods with whole grain crackers, fruit, vegetables, whole wheat pasta, grains, and nuts\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-6-How-to-Heal-a-Leaky-Gut-with-Diet.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-heal-a-leaky-gut-with-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Heal a Leaky Gut with Diet</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The recommended diet for leaky gut treatment. Which foods and food components can boost the integrity of our intestinal barrier?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-dr-greger-in-the-kitchen-my-new-favorite-beverage/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70092\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/10/DrG-in-the-kitchen-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"picture of Dr. Greger\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/10/DrG-in-the-kitchen-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/10/DrG-in-the-kitchen-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/10/DrG-in-the-kitchen-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/10/DrG-in-the-kitchen-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/10/DrG-in-the-kitchen-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/10/DrG-in-the-kitchen-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/10/DrG-in-the-kitchen-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/10/DrG-in-the-kitchen.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-dr-greger-in-the-kitchen-my-new-favorite-beverage/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Flashback Friday: Dr. Greger in the Kitchen—My New Favorite Beverage</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I blend up a vegetable smoothie inspired by a recipe in </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The How Not to Die Cookbook</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
